+Re-encoding all $T=19$ frames at every decision would multiply the
+encoder cost by 19. Instead, each frame is encoded once and the window
+is assembled from buffered vectors,
+\begin{equation}
+\bm z_t=f_\theta(\tilde{x}_t)\in\mathbb R^D,\qquad
+\bm Z_t=[\bm z_{t-T+1}^{\mathsf T};\ldots;\bm z_t^{\mathsf T}]
+\in\mathbb R^{T\times D}.
+\label{eq:buffer}
+\end{equation}
+An event with more than five unresolved frames is excluded; for every
+remaining event, $m_j\in\{0,1\}$ records whether window position $j$ is
+valid. The head uses three residual 1-D Conv--BatchNorm--ReLU layers
+with kernel size 3 and dilations $d_\ell\in\{1,2,4\}$:
+\begin{equation}
+\bm h_j^{(\ell)}=\operatorname{ReLU}\!\left(\operatorname{BN}_\ell\!\left(
+\sum_{q=-1}^{1}\bm W_q^{(\ell)}
+ [m_{j-d_\ell q}\bm h_{j-d_\ell q}^{(\ell-1)}]
++\bm b^{(\ell)}\right)\right)+\bm h_j^{(\ell-1)},
+\label{eq:tcn}
+\end{equation}
+where $\bm h_j^{(0)}=\bm z_j$ and out-of-window indices are zero-padded.
+The mask is applied before every convolution and masked positions are
+excluded from both pooling operations,
+\begin{equation}
+\bm h_{\mathrm{avg}}=\frac{\sum_jm_j\bm h_j^{(3)}}{\max(1,\sum_jm_j)},\quad
+\bm h_{\mathrm{max}}=\max_{j:m_j=1}\bm h_j^{(3)},\quad
+p=\varsigma\!\left(\operatorname{MLP}([\,\bm h_{\mathrm{avg}};\bm h_{\mathrm{max}}\,])\right).
+\label{eq:pooling}
+\end{equation}
+The MLP has a 32-dimensional input, a 64-unit ReLU layer with dropout
+0.3, and one logit output. Symmetric padding means that a position can
+use later positions within its already collected window; the deployed
+decision nevertheless requires no frames beyond the current buffer. The
+head costs 0.0459~MMAC per stride-1 decision, 0.37\% of the 12.49~MMAC
+per-frame model total. A 512-dimensional feature map would raise this
+head cost to 2.36~MMAC.
+
+\subsection{Reference Formulation and Decision Criterion}
+For the EAR-rule baseline, $\mathrm{EAR}_j$ is the mean EAR of both eyes
+at valid position $j$. Let $j_f$ and $j_l$ be the first and last valid
+positions in the window. We use the relative drop
+\begin{equation}
+r_t=1-\frac{\min_{j:m_j=1}\mathrm{EAR}_j}
+{[\mathrm{EAR}_{j_f}+\mathrm{EAR}_{j_l}]/2},
+\label{eq:earrule}
+\end{equation}
+and select its classification threshold on the validation fold. For a
+reference method, $\Delta=\mathrm{PR\mbox{-}AUC}_{\mathrm{ours}}-
+\mathrm{PR\mbox{-}AUC}_{\mathrm{ref}}$ is non-inferior when the lower
+limit of its paired 95\% confidence interval exceeds $-\delta$, with
+$\delta=0.02$ specified before the final comparisons.
 
